  @case 'springs: the pull is charged over the window half it lies in'  [pure]  @ 636-645
  @case 'relax: a pair settles where the hand solution puts it'  [pure]  @ 649-659
  @case 'relax: the springs press a strand to its window edge'  [pure]  @ 663-675
  @case 'relax: a comma loop spreads its residue across the springs'  [pure]  @ 679-712
  @case 'relax: a warm start settles where the cold one did'  [pure]  @ 716-732
  @case 'relax: a held strand stands where it was put, and the rest settle around it'  [pure]  @ 736-762
  @case 'spellings: a major triad comes back spelled as the theory table has it'  [pure]  @ 766-779
  @case 'spellings: a sonority no chain connects is refused'  [pure]  @ 783-802
  @case 'spellings: the offset is the spelling\'s, so which member anchors decides nothing'  [pure]  @ 806-824
  @case 'spellings: every spelling ties the whole sonority, silence pricing under any answer'  [pure]  @ 828-851
  @case 'spellings: the windows hold the stretch between them, or no spelling does'  [pure]  @ 855-875
  @case 'spellings: a rolled minor defers rather than state what the chord has not'  [pure]  @ 879-897
  @case 'spellings: a width of infinity is the enumeration the beam is checked against'  [pure]  @ 901-915
  @case 'spellings: the cut runs within a waiting set, not across them'  [pure]  @ 919-936
  @case 'spellings: seats, windows and waits are read at the strand a member names'  [pure]  @ 940-956
  @case 'seats: the notation gives each strand its step and the reach either side'  [pure]  @ 960-976
  @case 'onsets: a member waits while an onset it sounds through is still to come'  [pure]  @ 980-996
  @case 'onsets: a member held by recency has stopped, so it is joined to and does not wait'  [pure]  @ 1000-1014
  @case 'search: the walk returns what an exhaustive search over its spelling lists returns'  [pure]  @ 1018-1039
  @case 'search: carrying one answer takes the greedy road'  [pure]  @ 1043-1058
  @case 'search: a strand that has stopped stands where the walk left it'  [pure]  @ 1062-1091
  @case 'search: a rolled chord lands where the struck chord lands'  [pure]  @ 1095-1109
  @case 'search: a deferral moves the charge rather than dodging it'  [pure]  @ 1113-1135
  @case 'search: a held sonority is charged in its own onset's slot'  [pure]  @ 1139-1151
  @case 'search: the road that pays as it goes is the road the walk keeps'  [pure]  @ 1155-1168
  @case 'search: a wait resolving to what its sonority offered is no second road'  [pure]  @ 1172-1185
  @case 'search: the cut runs over the answers that owe and the answers that have paid'  [pure]  @ 1189-1201
  @case 'strands: a class chains through its overlaps and splits where they stop'  [pure]  @ 1205-1222
  @case 'strands: classes never share one, and the order does not follow the input'  [pure]  @ 1226-1239
  @case 'a block chord and an arpeggio of it hand back the same set'  [pure]  @ 1243-1255
  @case 'at n one above the arity consecutive sonorities still overlap'  [pure]  @ 1259-1273
  @case 'a repeated note and an octave doubling each spend one entry'  [pure]  @ 1277-1292
  @case 'a later strand of a class replaces the earlier one'  [pure]  @ 1296-1308
  @case 'a class still sounding stands where the last n struck have dropped it'  [pure]  @ 1312-1325
