  @case 'the C7's two sevenths cross at a pull of 0.95'  [pure]  @ 1364-1386
  @case 'the solve is the minimum exhaustive enumeration finds'  [pure]  @ 1390-1402
  @case 'a shortlist of one is fixed and still contributes its coords'  [pure]  @ 1406-1427
  @case 'a held strand bends the harmony to it'  [pure]  @ 1431-1453
  @case 'behind a run of fixed classes the answer hangs on the hold'  [pure]  @ 1457-1463
  @case 'the C7 sounding alone crosses at a pull of 0.95'  [pure]  @ 1467-1489
  @case 'the rest of the chord stands still, and the third seventh is dominated'  [pure]  @ 1493-1507
  @case 'resolving to F–A–C the seventh takes the Pythagorean under any pull'  [pure]  @ 1511-1529
  @case 'at n one above the arity the resolution reads the seventh chord's bass alone'  [pure]  @ 1533-1551
  @case 'an exact tie goes to the first candidate rather than to table order'  [pure]  @ 1555-1575
  @case 'an empty shortlist and an unaffordable solve are both refused'  [pure]  @ 1579-1592

